      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #10910.\n\nUse fsspec's path-only `ls(..., detail=False)` for cloud JSON directories instead of assuming every detailed entry has an S3-specific `Key`. Standard listings use `name`, so the old code raises `KeyError` before reading any files.\n\nKeep the existing JSON/JSONL filter, concatenation, and single-file behavior. Tests use a real fsspec in-memory filesystem through the existing filesystem-creation boundary, covering S3/GS/GCS path forms, mixed JSON/JSONL directories, unrelated files, and the intended no-JSON error.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Original code: 4 regression failures / 6 passing controls.\n- Fixed cloud-loader and existing converter tests: 12 passed, repeated.\n- Changed-file Ruff lint/format, license checks, and diff checks pass; source distribution and wheel build successfully.\n- Repository-wide `make quality` stops on an existing W293 whitespace issue in the unchanged model patcher. That unrelated file is not changed here; full model/training suites and real cloud-provider integration were not run.\n\nAgent-assisted contribution; no new runtime dependencies or model/cloud API calls.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the contributor guideline?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
